\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The three-arm replay at one interaction point. The recorded prefix is forced up to the harness decision $h_t$; each arm changes exactly one thing (the harness decision, the model action, or both) and runs live from there. Interaction is $I = C_{HM} - C_H - C_M$; \emph  {screening-off} is the event $C_{HM} = C_M$ --- the joint arm collapses onto the model arm, so the harness flip adds nothing beyond the model's alternative.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method}{{1}{4}{The three-arm replay at one interaction point. The recorded prefix is forced up to the harness decision $h_t$; each arm changes exactly one thing (the harness decision, the model action, or both) and runs live from there. Interaction is $I = C_{HM} - C_H - C_M$; \emph {screening-off} is the event $C_{HM} = C_M$ --- the joint arm collapses onto the model arm, so the harness flip adds nothing beyond the model's alternative}{figure.1}{}}
